    {
      "_id": "2869d659457e4921",
      "name": "Thaumaturgy — 3 Advanced — Way of the Stone",
      "type": "power",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>The vampire transforms himself into what resembles a stone dolmen, becoming immune to daylight and fire and capable of a very limited amount of movement &mdash; the source of legends of stones that walk at night. His features grow indistinct, taking on a semi-carved aspect, and the difficulty for all physical actions increases by two while movement drops to one-quarter normal.</p><p><strong>System:</strong> The vampire allows three blood points' worth of his blood to drain onto a boulder, assuming its rough shape and consistency. Successes on a Willpower roll (difficulty 7) determine how long he may remain in stone form, from one turn (1 success) up to one month (6+ successes); he may abort the effect early if he wishes.</p>",
        "source": "Libellus Sanguinis II: Keepers of the Word, Book Two: Usurpers",
